// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Copy to `Local.xcconfig` (gitignored) if you need to change either value:
//
//     cp Config/Local.xcconfig.example Config/Local.xcconfig
//
// There is no API key to put here. Muraka depends on no keyed service at all — that
// is a hard project constraint, not an oversight.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ── Running against a dev stack from a PHYSICAL iPhone ──────────────────────
// The simulator reaches the Mac on localhost; a phone cannot. Use the Mac's LAN
// address, which `ipconfig getifaddr en0` prints.
//
// Remember the xcconfig comment gotcha: `//` starts a comment anywhere on a line, so
// the slashes must come from $(SLASH).
//
// SLASH = /
// MURAKA_API_BASE_URL = http:$(SLASH)$(SLASH)192.168.1.20:8090

// ── Running on a physical iPhone at all ─────────────────────────────────────
// Your team ID is the ten-character code under Xcode → Settings → Accounts →
// (your Apple ID) → Manage Certificates. A free Apple ID has one.
//
// It belongs here rather than in project.yml because `xcodegen generate` rewrites the
// project, so anything set in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities editor is lost on the
// next regeneration. Set here, it survives.
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345

// Bundle identifiers are unique across every Apple developer account, so `mv.muraka`
// cannot be signed by anyone else's team. Claim your own.
//
// MURAKA_BUNDLE_ID = com.yourname.muraka
